                <a:cs typeface="Arial" panose="020B0604020202090204" pitchFamily="34" charset="-120"/>
            </a:rPr><a:t>AI models can produce diverse proposals on paper, but that diversity operates within a different conceptual space than humans. Human scientists bring genuinely novel perspectives &#8212; ideas further from published literature and outside the semantic territory AI models inhabit. This suggests AI is better positioned as an ideation complement to, rather than replacement for, human researchers.</a:t></a:r>
